      "purpose": "Rank revolutionary artists by the gap between outward and inward closeness",
      "base_or_modification": "modification",
      "summary": "A revolutionary artist is defined as one who influences many and is influenced by few. Out-closeness and in-closeness are computed on the directed network and combined into one score. The top twelve include Bob Dylan, Chuck Berry and the Beatles. The definition is checked by redefining similarity relative to the central node, which drops the mean from about 0.85 to about 0.45 as predicted. Low-frequency content of the trait series is then read with a discrete Fourier transform.",
